itations and sometimes it  does right but also if you really love  something you can find a way to be part  of it  and to learn about it despite not having  money because the knowledge thankfully  with the internet and everything that we  have is more available and technically  kind of free  I saw your stand-up special and you're  like okay guys for those of you who  don't know what an encyclopedia it's the  Internet in books it's so weird it's so  weird I'm at that age now where I talk  about the technology I grew up with and  then people were like what is that like  the VCR you get to the point where you  even say MySpace and people are like  what what is that is that like tik-tok  but quicker like and you're just like oh  my god like myspace was a thing not too  long ago but now it's like obsolete you  know so how do you grapple with the fact  that you grew up you say a lot in the  book a latchkey kid home alone for hours  on end and and TV was your first friend  right keeping you company you formed  relationships with the with the four  Golden Girls you were the fit yeah your  mind yeah so like now you had your own  TV show Christina you're providing that  representation you're now in you were in  people's living rooms you do this but  they're stand-up and now your book how  does that feel for you to be providing  that comfort that companionship for you  know like you I think that when we talk  there's a lot of talk especially  especially right now with Hispanic  Heritage Month we talk about  representation being important in TV and  film and on screen but I also say that  it's important to do it behind the  screen too because if we don't have  decision makers that that understand the  journey it's hard to actually have a  journey to you know to tell for me  everything I do and it's not for  everybody but my journey has always been  to tell my story and give the  programming that little me would have  loved to have seen so for me you know my  show was cancelled 